.TH SDL_GetRendererProperties 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetRendererProperties \- Get the properties associated with a renderer.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_PropertiesID SDL_GetRendererProperties(SDL_Renderer *renderer);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The following read-only properties are provided by SDL:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_NAME_STRING :
the name of the rendering driver
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_WINDOW_POINTER :
the window where rendering is displayed, if any
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_SURFACE_POINTER :
the surface where rendering is displayed, if this is a software renderer without a window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_VSYNC_NUMBER :
the current vsync setting
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE_NUMBER :
the maximum texture width and height
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_TEXTURE_FORMATS_POINTER :
a (const
.BR SDL_PixelFormat
*) array of pixel formats, terminated with
.BR SDL_PIXELFORMAT_UNKNOWN ,
representing the available texture formats for this renderer\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_TEXTURE_WRAPPING_BOOLEAN :
true if the renderer supports
.BR SDL_TEXTURE_ADDRESS_WRAP
on non-power-of-two textures\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_OUTPUT_COLORSPACE_NUMBER :
an
.BR SDL_Colorspace
value describing the colorspace for output to the display, defaults to
.BR SDL_COLORSPACE_SRGB \[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_HDR_ENABLED_BOOLEAN :
true if the output colorspace is
.BR SDL_COLORSPACE_SRGB_LINEAR
and the renderer is showing on a display with HDR enabled\[char46] This property can change dynamically when
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_HDR_STATE_CHANGED
is sent\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_SDR_WHITE_POINT_FLOAT :
the value of SDR white in the
.BR SDL_COLORSPACE_SRGB_LINEAR
colorspace\[char46] When HDR is enabled, this value is automatically multiplied into the color scale\[char46] This property can change dynamically when
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_HDR_STATE_CHANGED
is sent\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_HDR_HEADROOM_FLOAT :
the additional high dynamic range that can be displayed, in terms of the SDR white point\[char46] When HDR is not enabled, this will be 1\[char46]0\[char46] This property can change dynamically when
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_HDR_STATE_CHANGED
is sent\[char46]
.PP
With the direct3d renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_D3D9_DEVICE_POINTER :
the IDirect3DDevice9 associated with the renderer
.PP
With the direct3d11 renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_D3D11_DEVICE_POINTER :
the ID3D11Device associated with the renderer
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_D3D11_SWAPCHAIN_POINTER :
the IDXGISwapChain1 associated with the renderer\[char46] This may change when the window is resized\[char46]
.PP
With the direct3d12 renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_D3D12_DEVICE_POINTER :
the ID3D12Device associated with the renderer
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_D3D12_SWAPCHAIN_POINTER :
the IDXGISwapChain4 associated with the renderer\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_D3D12_COMMAND_QUEUE_POINTER :
the ID3D12CommandQueue associated with the renderer
.PP
With the metal renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_METAL_DEVICE_POINTER :
the MTLDevice associated with the renderer
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_METAL_COMMAND_QUEUE_POINTER :
the MTLCommandQueue associated with the renderer\[char46] Work submitted on this queue will be ordered relative to other rendering\[char46]
.BR SDL_FlushRenderer ()
can be used to guarantee the current rendering has been submitted\[char46]
.PP
With the vulkan renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_VULKAN_INSTANCE_POINTER :
the VkInstance associated with the renderer
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_VULKAN_SURFACE_NUMBER :
the VkSurfaceKHR associated with the renderer
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_VULKAN_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_POINTER :
the VkPhysicalDevice associated with the renderer
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_VULKAN_DEVICE_POINTER :
the VkDevice associated with the renderer
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_VULKAN_GRAPHICS_QUEUE_FAMILY_INDEX_NUMBER :
the queue family index used for rendering
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_VULKAN_PRESENT_QUEUE_FAMILY_INDEX_NUMBER :
the queue family index used for presentation
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_VULKAN_SWAPCHAIN_IMAGE_COUNT_NUMBER :
the number of swapchain images, or potential frames in flight, used by the Vulkan renderer
.PP
With the gpu renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_RENDERER_GPU_DEVICE_POINTER :
the
.BR SDL_GPUDevice
associated with the renderer

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the rendering context\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a valid property ID on success or 0 on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

